      "deletions": 1,
      "changed_files": 1
    },
    {
      "number": 930,
      "title": "pm: move Projects and Tasks into Wave-owned Linear teams",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```bash\nlf pm init --wave product --team-key PRD\nlf pm reteam --wave product\nlf pm reteam --wave product --apply\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nMakes one Linear team the explicit owner of each Wave. Projects move before their open Issues; dormant Task Sessions adopt Linear's reassigned identifier atomically, while a writing Task body defers safely. Linear Project titles show the Wave prefix without changing Loopflow's canonical Project slug.\n\n## Changes\n\n- rebind an existing Wave with an explicit team key or name\n- move Projects onto the Wave team before Issues\n- migrate waiting, blocked, and failed Tasks while protecting active writers\n- preserve concise Loopflow Project names and slugs behind Wave-prefixed Linear titles\n- leave completed W2 issues historical so shipped references stay stable",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 579,
      "deletions": 91,
      "changed_files": 9
    },
    {
      "number": 931,
      "title": "lf: open the desktop app by default",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```bash\nlf              # open or focus Loopflow.app\nlf desktop      # explicit alias\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nBare `lf` now opens the primary Loopflow application instead of launching an implicit vendor session. Agent work requires a named skill, flow, or inline prompt. The canonical migration chain also restores `0.11.006_context_launch_work` before `.007`, so databases written by the Context Lab build remain readable by current releases.",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 63,
      "deletions": 9,
